course: dictionary
lesson: 13763
title: Interpretation: what does it mean?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An interpretation is someone's explanation of what something means. Two people can read the same poem and have different interpretations of it. The word comes from «interpret», which means to explain or make sense of something.
explain: «My interpretation of the poem is that the moon is a lonely friend.» Here the reader says what she thinks the poem means. Her idea is one way to understand it, not the only way.
explain: Interpretation can also mean the way a performer shows something. «The actor's interpretation of the villain was cold and quiet.» Actors, singers and musicians each give their own interpretation of the same script or song.
explain: Interpretation can also mean turning spoken words into another language. «The interpretation of the speech into French was clear and fast.» The clues are speech and French, so here it means translating.
fact: An interpretation is an explanation of what something means.
fact: «Interpretation» comes from «interpret», which means to explain or make sense of something.
fact: In maths and science, an interpretation of a graph means saying what the graph shows.
fact: An interpreter turns spoken words from one language into another.
fact: Good readers support their interpretation with evidence from the text.
exercise: «After reading the poem, Sam gave his interpretation of the final line.» What is an interpretation? | *An explanation of what something means | A rough sketch of a tree | A type of drum | A fast race
exercise: «The graph goes up each week, so my interpretation is that sales are growing.» In this sentence, what does the interpretation say? | The name of the teacher | How long the graph took to draw | *What the graph shows | The colour of the graph
exercise: Maya hears someone speak Spanish and tells her friend the words in English. What job is she doing? | Painting a picture | Singing in a choir | Measuring a room | *Interpreting
test: «The drama teacher asked each actor for a fresh interpretation of the character.» What does a fresh interpretation of a character mean? | Copying the last actor exactly | Forgetting all the lines | *A new way of performing and showing the character | Sitting down quietly
test: What does an interpreter do? | Plays the piano in a band | *Turns spoken words from one language into another | Paints pictures in a gallery | Explains the rules of a game
exam: «Two readers gave different interpretations of the same poem, and both had good reasons.» What does this tell you? | Only one reader can ever be right | Interpretations are always exactly the same | *A text can have more than one reasonable interpretation | The poem must be very short
